-- title:
--   Frobenius squared is the inverse diamond at supersingular places
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $M/p$ nonzero, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume that the $q$-series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the function field $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of Laurent series generated by the integral form ratios of full level. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model at $p$ of the level-$H$ curve in the sense of the structure `XHDRModelAtP` (properness, flatness, integrality, normality of the level-$\Gamma_M$ model, smoothness of relative dimension one of the level-$\Gamma_N$ model, an identification of the geometric fibre with a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with $q$-expansions, Galois equivariance, diamond automorphisms, and the remaining fields of that structure). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be a ring homomorphism inducing the structural map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ after composing with the inclusion of $A$. Assume the hypothesis `hdia0`: for each unit $e$ of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ and each closed point $P$ of the curve underlying the special fibre model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}\,A\,\rho$, the point obtained from $P$ by transporting along the fibre identification `efib`, applying the fibre map of the diamond automorphism $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{dia0}\,e$ over the residue map $\kappa$-reduction of $\rho$, and transporting back, is again closed, and its associated place is the translate of the place of $P$ under the semilinear automorphism `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut` attached to the algebra automorphism $\mathrm{diamondActionModL}\,\kappa\,(M/p)\,(\mathrm{infSubgroup}\,p\,M\,H)$ evaluated at a $\Gamma_0(M/p)$-lift of $e$. Let $pb$ be a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ whose underlying class is $p$, and let $y$ be a place of `qExpFunctionFieldC κ (ΓN p M H hpM)` over $\kappa$ lying in the supersingular set `ssPlacesQExp κ (ΓN p M H hpM) p`. The conclusion is that the translate of the Frobenius place $\mathrm{Frob}(y) :=$ `qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL κ (ΓN p M H hpM) p y` (the restriction of $y$ along the integral mod-$p$ Frobenius endomorphism of that function field) by the semilinear automorphism attached to $\mathrm{diamondActionModL}$ at a $\Gamma_0(M/p)$-lift of $pb$ again lies in `ssPlacesQExp κ (ΓN p M H hpM) p`, and that $\mathrm{Frob}$ of this translate is $y$.
--
--   This is the relation $\mathrm{Frob}^2 = \langle p \rangle^{-1}$ on the supersingular places of the special fibre at $p$ of the modular curve, in the form: $\langle p \rangle_{*}\mathrm{Frob}$ is an involution of the supersingular set, read off from the model rather than from moduli of elliptic curves. It feeds the analysis of the special fibre of the Jacobian, where it is used in the identification of the Hecke operator $U_p$ with Frobenius and Verschiebung on the character group attached to the supersingular points.
